   "evidence": "`grep -n '\\.EPS'` over `EpsilonEridani/` matches only the field declaration at Spin.lean:78; no occurrence of `K.EPS`. Every field consumed from `K` (`K.p`, `K.q`, `K.S`, `K.M2 g`, `K.xBj g`, `K.Q2 g`) is already available on `PolarizedKinematics` (Polarized/Kinematics.lean:66-72 plus `DisKinematics`), so the parent record suffices verbatim. Roadmap SpinStructure/README.md \u00a70.2 keeps `\u03b5` a parameter and Convention 5 names `PolarizedKinematics` as the record.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Polarized/Spin.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `SpinKinematics` (and its `@[ext]`) and take `K : PolarizedKinematics g` with `EPS` as the explicit parameter, matching the roadmap's `IsG1G2Decomposition g K G W` shape; alternatively keep the structure and define `structureOne (K : SpinKinematics g) := K.EPS.bilinMap ![K.q, K.S]` with no separate `EPS` argument. Carrying both is what must go.",
   "issue": "`SpinKinematics` extends `PolarizedKinematics` solely with `EPS`, but that field is never used: `structureOne`/`structureTwo` and every lemma take an independent explicit `EPS` argument (lines 89, 92, 97, 100, 108, 113, 118, 123, 128, 133, 155, 167, 173). The declarations therefore require a strictly stronger record than they use, and the interface admits `structureOne EPS' K` with `EPS' \u2260 K.EPS`, so the orientation \"fixed once\" in `K` (Convention 4) does not in fact fix anything.",
   "line": "75"
  }
 ],
